# Skill execution (installed skills)

Task is **not** complete until:

| Skill | Done when |
|-------|-----------|
| **excalidraw-diagram** | `.excalidraw` → PNG rendered, images **viewed**, layout fixed |
| **word-document** | DOCX validates; explicit table styling (docx-js) or one python-docx path; deliver **`.docx` only** (no generator beside deliverable unless user asks) |
| **word-document (no npm)** | python-docx + `validate`; note fallback in reply; `bash scripts/install_deps.sh office` |
| **powerpoint-presentation** | PPTX validates; **`thumbnail` every deck** (grid + `--per-slide` 150 DPI), images **viewed**, overflow fixed; `office-system` installed if missing |
| **powerpoint-presentation (no npm)** | Template/XML path only — **no** greenfield deck; do not claim new-deck delivery without pptxgenjs or user template; preview still mandatory if `.pptx` delivered |
| **spreadsheet-document** | `.xlsx` delivered; if formulas used: `office_tools.py recalc` → JSON `status: success` (zero formula errors); `office-system` for recalc |
| **pdf-document** | Deliver requested `.pdf`; form fills: run validation scripts per `references/forms.md` |
| **verification-before-completion** | No completion/success claim without fresh verification command output in the same message |
| **api-and-interface-design** | Contract defined before implementation; consistent errors; validation at boundaries; pagination on lists; cross-check against `deprecation-and-migration` when changing public interfaces |
| **deprecation-and-migration** | Replacement exists before deprecation; migration guide with concrete steps; usage verified at zero before removal; formal deliverables use `word-document` when requested |
| **terraform-commit-review** | Commit range established; every changed file read; provider docs verified via MCP (Context7 + Microsoft Learn); all 7 checklist sections applied (correctness, security/RBAC, destructive changes, naming, cross-phase, code quality, documentation/runbook); structured report with intent summary, per-phase table, issues by severity, vendor-ready comments, source URLs, and execution summary when no apply blockers |
| **terraform-apply-assistance** | Apply scope established (commit hash through HEAD or inferred); error/plan triaged; focused branch created or confirmed; diagnosis backed by Context7 + Microsoft Learn MCP; smallest correct edit applied; local validation run (fmt, validate, diff --check); **paused for user review** — no commit/push unless user explicitly instructs; plan evaluated with rubric (OK / conditionally OK / not OK); unresolved risks re-raised every iteration; execution summary with apply decision, prerequisites, phase order, and post-apply checks |

**PowerPoint is not done** when the `.pptx` exists—only after layout preview (or user waives visual QA).

Artifact skills (Word, PPT, XLSX, PDF) require **verification-before-completion** before delivery claims.

- **PPT:** LibreOffice Impress + Poppler every delivery → `bash scripts/install_deps.sh office-system`
- **Word (new):** `bash scripts/install_deps.sh node` for docx-js; without npm → python-docx via `bash scripts/install_deps.sh office`
- **PPT (new):** `bash scripts/install_deps.sh node` for pptxgenjs only — no python greenfield fallback
- **Excalidraw:** Playwright via `bash scripts/install_deps.sh excalidraw`

## Custom agents (installed library)

Applies when the user invokes a custom agent or you test agent behavior in this repo:

| Agent | Done when |
|-------|-----------|
| **code-review** | Scope established (SHA range when provided); tests reviewed first; five-axis review; requirements alignment when plan supplied; logic traced; Strengths + findings with file:line evidence; verification story; MCP/web verification table; merge verdict (Yes/No/With fixes); **no source files edited** |
| **security-auditor** | Scope established; trust boundaries + STRIDE; findings by severity with file:line evidence; PoC for Critical/High; MCP/web verification when applicable; release verdict (Yes/No/With fixes); **no source files edited** |

After editing `agents/`, run `bash scripts/install_library.sh agents cursor` so global `~/.cursor/agents/` matches repo source.

## Dependencies

| Target | Command | For |
|--------|---------|-----|
| Office Python | `bash scripts/install_deps.sh office` | validate, extract, unpack/pack |
| Excalidraw | `bash scripts/install_deps.sh excalidraw` | PNG render |
| LibreOffice + Poppler | `bash scripts/install_deps.sh office-system` | **all PPT deliveries**, XLSX `recalc`, DOCX `accept`, conversions |
| PDF Python (pypdf, etc.) | `bash scripts/install_deps.sh pdf` | pdf-document scripts |
| Node + npm globals | `bash scripts/install_deps.sh node` | new Word (docx-js) / new PPT (pptxgenjs) |
| python-docx | `bash scripts/install_deps.sh office` | Word fallback when npm missing |

## Office toolkit

```bash
cd skills/_shared/office-tools
uv run python3 office_tools.py validate deck.pptx --auto-repair
uv run python3 office_tools.py thumbnail deck.pptx /tmp/preview --cols 4
uv run python3 office_tools.py thumbnail deck.pptx /tmp/preview --per-slide /tmp/slides --dpi 150 --no-grid
```

PPT details: `skills/powerpoint-presentation/references/layout-preview.md`.
